{"id":17,"date":"2018-09-17T19:49:30","date_gmt":"2018-09-17T13:49:30","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/weis2020-2.econinfosec.org\/?page_id=17"},"modified":"2022-03-25T22:51:16","modified_gmt":"2022-03-25T16:51:16","slug":"sponsorship","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/sponsorship\/","title":{"rendered":"Sponsorship"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Thanks to:<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image is-resized\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.nsf.gov\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"http:\/\/weis2020-2.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo-1019x1024.png\" alt=\"National Science Foundation\" class=\"wp-image-113\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" srcset=\"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo-1019x1024.png 1019w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo-298x300.png 298w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo-768x772.png 768w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2019\/02\/NSF_4-Color_bitmap_Logo.png 1722w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" \/><\/a><figcaption>National Science Foundation<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Platinum Sponsor:<br><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1257\" height=\"487\" class=\"wp-image-582\" style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2022\/03\/mmclogo.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2022\/03\/mmclogo.jpg 1257w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2022\/03\/mmclogo-300x116.jpg 300w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2022\/03\/mmclogo-1024x397.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/10\/2022\/03\/mmclogo-768x298.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1257px) 100vw, 1257px\" \/><\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator\" \/>\n\n\n<h2>About WEIS<\/h2>\n<p>This year marks the 21st consecutive year of the Workshop on the Economics of Information Security (WEIS). The field of the economics of privacy and security has grown substantially since it first began. However, the workshop has remained the leading forum for interdisciplinary scholarship on information security, combining expertise from the fields of computer science and electrical engineering, economics, social science, business, law, and policy. Each year, WEIS is attended by 100-150 academic researchers, industry practitioners, policymakers, and graduate students.<\/p>\n<p>Sponsorship of WEIS helps the community by allowing us to keep registration costs low, while also demonstrating corporate commitment to information security research and innovation.<\/p>\n<h3>Why WEIS?<\/h3>\n<p>WEIS embodies\u00a0the idea that responding to security problems\u00a0through purely technical means is a losing strategy because it leads to\u00a0an arms race. Interdisciplinary research is needed: an understanding of attacker incentives, motivations, and behaviors is necessary to accurately model future attacks\u00a0so that information security professionals can\u00a0more effectively defend their systems. WEIS is also regularly attended by policymakers, because it\u00a0provides a forum for them to both understand how to craft more effective policies, as well as directly interact with those who their policies are likely to impact.<\/p>\n<h3>Benefits of Sponsorship<\/h3>\n<p>Sponsorship of WEIS provides the following benefits:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Demonstrate Thought Leadership:\u00a0<\/strong>By sponsoring WEIS, organizations demonstrate their commitment to improving information security systems, practices, and policies through innovative interdisciplinary research. WEIS sponsors are featured prominently on the public\u00a0website and\u00a0in the materials distributed to attendees (depending on sponsorship level).<\/li>\n<li><strong>Recruitment Opportunities: <\/strong>At its heart, WEIS is an academic workshop in which researchers present peer-reviewed studies on information security. As a result, WEIS is regularly attended by PhD students and professors. Many of these students are actively trying to make connections with industry in order to find internship opportunities, employment upon graduation, or collaboration opportunities.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Competitive Advantage:\u00a0<\/strong>WEIS attendees have access to cutting-edge research during the presentation sessions, as well as opportunities to network with the researchers during breaks and social events. This means that they are among the first to receive exposure to new information security research that can directly by applied to their organizations.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3>Levels of Sponsorship<\/h3>\n<p>WEIS sponsorship is available at\u00a0four levels:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Diamond ($25,000)<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Logo displayed on the public WEIS website<\/li>\n<li>Promotional materials included in registration packets<\/li>\n<li>8 complimentary WEIS registrations for your organization<\/li>\n<li>Signage on display in main workshop venue<\/li>\n<li>Sole industry workshop headline sponsor<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Platinum ($10,000)<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Logo displayed on the public WEIS website<\/li>\n<li>Promotional materials included in registration packets<\/li>\n<li>5 complimentary WEIS registrations for your organization<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Gold ($5,000)<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Logo displayed\u00a0on the public WEIS website<\/li>\n<li>Promotional materials included in registration packets<\/li>\n<li>3 complimentary WEIS registrations for your organization<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Silver ($2,000)<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Logo displayed\u00a0on the public WEIS website<\/li>\n<li>1 complimentary WEIS registration for your organization<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3>Interested in Sponsorship?<\/h3>\n<p>To pursue sponsorship opportunities, please contact the 2022 WEIS chairs:<\/p>\n<p>tyler-moore@utulsa.edu<\/p>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Thanks to: Platinum Sponsor: About WEIS This year marks the 21st consecutive year of the Workshop on the Economics of Information Security (WEIS). The field of the economics of privacy and security has grown substantially since it first began. However, the workshop has remained the leading forum for interdisciplinary scholarship on information security, combining expertise [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":5,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":7,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-17","page","type-page","status-publish","czr-hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/17","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/5"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=17"}],"version-history":[{"count":25,"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/17\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":587,"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/17\/revisions\/587"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/weis2022.econinfosec.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=17"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}"